---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy – FutureMedia" bodyClass="legal-page">
<main class="legal">
  <div class="legal-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Future Media</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>How we collect, use and protect personal information on futuremedia.com.na - and the terms that govern use of this website.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="legal-block" id="privacy">
    <h2>Our commitment</h2>
    <p>Future Media (“Future Media,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) is committed to protecting the privacy and security of the personal information we collect from visitors, clients and prospective partners through this website (futuremedia.com.na). This policy outlines our practices concerning the information we collect and how we use and safeguard that information.</p>

    <article>
      <h3>1. Information we collect</h3>
      <p>We limit the collection of personal information to what is necessary to fulfil your requests for contact, media planning, applications or document access. Depending on the form you use, the information we collect may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Telephone number</li>
        <li>Company name and role</li>
        <li>Brand, sales need or service preferences</li>
        <li>Application details and CV uploads (vacancies / freelancers)</li>
        <li>Campaign or media-audit answers you choose to share</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>2. How we use your information</h3>
      <p>The personal information collected through this website is used exclusively for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Service provision:</strong> to process and respond to your direct inquiries and communication requests.</li>
        <li><strong>Media planning:</strong> to recommend advertising, conference, brand or digital solutions based on the information you submit.</li>
        <li><strong>Applications:</strong> to review vacancy and freelancer submissions and follow up with candidates.</li>
        <li><strong>Document delivery:</strong> to email gated briefings or company materials you request.</li>
        <li><strong>Administration:</strong> for internal administrative, analytical and record-keeping purposes.</li>
        <li><strong>Regulatory compliance:</strong> to comply with any applicable legal or regulatory requirements.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>3. Data storage and security</h3>
      <p>We recognise the sensitive nature of the information we collect.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>All personal data submitted through this website is stored securely in Future Media’s systems and trusted service providers used to operate the site.</li>
        <li>We maintain appropriate administrative, technical and physical safeguards designed to protect the information against accidental, unlawful or unauthorised destruction, loss, alteration, access, disclosure or use.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>4. Accounts and access</h3>
      <p>This public website does not feature a general user portal for clients to manage media bookings online. Where admin tools exist for Future Media staff, access is restricted and authenticated. Visitors are not required to create accounts or passwords to browse the site or submit a form.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>5. Disclosure of information</h3>
      <p>We will not sell, rent or trade your personal information. We may disclose your information only to the extent necessary to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Route your enquiry to the right Future Media brand, sales or production team.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations, regulatory bodies or government authorities.</li>
        <li>Protect the rights, property or safety of Future Media, our clients or the public.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>6. Contact us</h3>
      <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how your personal information is handled, please contact us:</p>
      <ul class="legal-contact">
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:sales@futuremedia.com.na">sales@futuremedia.com.na</a></li>
        <li>Telephone: <a href="tel:+264830001000">+264 83 000 1000</a></li>
        <li>Address: Unit 44, Hyper Motor City, Maxwell Street, Windhoek</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" id="terms">
    <h2>Terms of use</h2>
    <p>Welcome to the official website of Future Media. The following Terms of Use govern your access to and use of our website (futuremedia.com.na). By accessing or using this website, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Use.</p>

    <article>
      <h3>1. Acceptance of terms</h3>
      <p>By using this website, you acknowledge that you have read, understood and agreed to these Terms of Use and our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, you must discontinue use of this website immediately.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>2. Use of website</h3>
      <p>This website is provided for informational purposes related to Future Media’s broadcast, digital, conference and advertising brands, and for initiating contact, media audits, applications or document requests.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You agree not to use the website for any unlawful purpose or in any way that violates these Terms of Use.</li>
        <li>You agree not to use any automated means (such as bots or scripts) to access, screen scrape or interfere with the operation of the website.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>3. Accuracy of information</h3>
      <p>While Future Media makes every effort to ensure the information on this website is current and accurate, we do not guarantee the completeness or accuracy of the information provided.</p>
      <p>Brand descriptions, audience figures, offers and event details are provided for general information and may change. Formal media plans, rates and contracts remain subject to written confirmation from Future Media.</p>
      <p>By submitting information through any form on this site, you warrant that the details you provide are accurate, current and complete.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>4. Intellectual property</h3>
      <p>All content on this website, including text, graphics, images, logos, brand names and the website design, is the exclusive property of Future Media or its licensors and is protected by copyright, trademark and other intellectual property laws.</p>
      <p>You may not reproduce, distribute, modify or use any content from this site without our prior written permission.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>5. Limitation of liability</h3>
      <p>The Future Media website is provided on an “as is” and “as available” basis. To the fullest extent permitted by law, Future Media disclaims all warranties. Future Media will not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential damages resulting from your use or inability to use the website or any content, products or services available through the site.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>6. Governing law</h3>
      <p>These Terms of Use shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Namibia. Any dispute arising out of or related to the use of this website shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of Namibia.</p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>7. Changes to terms</h3>
      <p>Future Media reserves the right to revise and update these Terms of Use and the Privacy Policy at any time without prior notice. Continued use of the website following any such changes constitutes your acceptance of the revised terms.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</main>
</Layout>
